  "term": "fertility",
  "definition": "Fertility is the capacity to produce a relatively large number of offspring through sexual reproduction. In this historical usage, it can refer either to the number of fertilized germ cells produced or, more meaningfully for population survival, to the number of offspring that live long enough to become reproductively mature.",
